The Story of Chinese Characters (汉字的故事) — Chalkboard (Lemo-Opuscar) · LemoLab × Claude Opus 5.5

IMAGES, FOOTAGE, MODELS
- None. The classroom wall, boards, frame, tray, clock, chalk and wet streak are drawn in code (js/stage.js, js/chalk.js,
  js/app.js). No photographs, no scans, no AI-generated images, no 3D models.

CHALK WRITING
- Every Chinese character written on the board is our own stroke data (js/hz.js): a centre line and a stroke type per
  stroke, in GF 0023-2020 stroke order, drawn by the chalk engine. While writing the data, proportions were checked by eye
  against LXGW WenKai set behind it (check page: index.html?lab=hz); no outline was copied or traced.
- The oracle-bone, bronze and seal forms of 射 are redrawn by hand as chalk lines (js/ancient.js); no ancient-script font.
  What they were drawn after is in FACTS.md.

FONTS (SIL Open Font License 1.1; licence texts in fonts/; not in git, build.sh downloads them)
- EMS Delight (teacher's English on the board) and EMS Casual Hand (the child's English), single-stroke SVG fonts:
  derivatives of Delius (Natalia Raices) and Covered By Your Grace (Kimberly Geswein); SVG conversion by Sheldon B.
  Michaels and Windell H. Oskay, gitlab.com/oskay/svg-fonts. fonts/OFL-EMS.txt
- LXGW WenKai v1.530 (© LXGW, github.com/lxgw/LxgwWenKai): the subtitle face, subset by tools/subset.py to the characters
  the subtitles use (fonts/wenkai-sub.woff2); the full font is used only on the check page. fonts/OFL-LXGWWenKai.txt

VOICE
- Chinese: Edge TTS (Microsoft), zh-CN-XiaoxiaoNeural, +15 %. English version: en-US-AvaNeural, +10 %.
  Through the library's core/tts/tts_zh.py; checked with core/tts/asr_check.py (faster-whisper, MIT; Whisper models, MIT).

